1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,957
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,687
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,917
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,537
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,677
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,877
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:55,717
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,040
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,617
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,020
We live in wonder.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,177
I'm gonna share them with
you, our love's so true.

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,577
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,777
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:32,057
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,737
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,780
We don't even want to do it.

26
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,780
Tony's acting as a decoy?

27
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,097
Don't worry, he'll be fine.

28
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,337
He's buying us some time.

29
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:56,137
But we've got to hurry!

30
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,380
Take me to Luffy and the others.

31
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,240
Sure, but Sanji, I thought
you got shot earlier?

32
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,150
Hello?

33
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,657
We've got him, sir.

34
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:15,377
And don't worry, he
won't be going anywhere?

35
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,020
So where are you?

36
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:21,917
Speak up I'm at the front of the big
casino with the alligator on top.

37
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,900
And rain base, rain dinners?

38
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:25,850
Nice job.

39
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:28,697
That was such a convincing performance
that your boss is on the way.

40
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:31,486
You should really consider
a career in acting.

41
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:32,610
Really?

42
00:02:32,693 --> 00:02:33,523
Gee, thanks!

43
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:36,277
Hey, um, you're gonna
let me go now, right?

44
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,200
No, sir.

45
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,680
Yeah, I didn't think so.

46
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,937
More of those millions creeps
are checking out our handiwork.

47
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:46,997
You better get going.

48
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,786
You know what to do, Chopper?

49
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,760
Who are you supposed to be?

50
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,800
My name is Mr. Prince.

51
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:58,017
Did you see who did this to our friends?

52
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,218
Hey, wait a minute.

53
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,280
Was it you?

54
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,833
Did you take them down?

55
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,860
Whatever I can manage.

56
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:06,837
Yes, I did it!

57
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,660
It was me, Mr. Prince!

58
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,237
My name's Mr.

59
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,100
Prince, you are Mr. Prince!

60
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,180
What the hell?

61
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,120
A guy.

62
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,320
He was called Mr. Prince.

63
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:40,700
I see.

64
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,860
The bridge collapsed!

65
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:55,640
The bridge to the casino just collapsed!

66
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,997
That's how Chopper and
I did it, more or less.

67
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,040
But is Tony going to be alright?

68
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:14,631
Yeah, that little furball's
got a few tricks up his sleeve.

69
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,540
You bastard.

70
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:23,620
I know you're here somewhere, Mr. Prince.

71
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:29,900
When I find you, I'm going
to introduce you to my hook.

72
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:32,477
Please don't notice me.

73
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,537
Please don't notice me.

74
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,973
Please don't notice me.

75
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,317
All of us are going to die!

76
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,106
The water's going to be
up to our next minute!

77
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,330
Hey!

78
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,120
Hey! Hey!

79
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:45,440
Hey, you stupid Katorea!

80
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,697
If you're hungry, come and get me!

81
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:48,797
Are you nuts, Nami?

82
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:49,998
What are you doing?

83
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:56,277
I'm trying to lure that Katorea in close
enough so he'll bite this cage apart!

84
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,190
Hey!

85
00:04:57,273 --> 00:04:58,174
That's not a bad idea!

86
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,657
Yeah, come and get us, you stupid banana!

87
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,800
You rotten banana!

88
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:05,480
Look, I told you, that
thing's not a banana.

89
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,037
It's an alligator with a
banana growing out of its head.

90
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,100
But it's called a banana Katorea.

91
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,297
Let me explain it to you.

92
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,857
You've heard of the monkey dance, right?

93
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:13,940
You don't banana!

94
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:16,442
Shut up and listen for a second!

95
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:20,237
Okay, look, there's a dance called
the monkey dance, you follow?

96
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:24,438
Even though it's got the word monkey
in it, it isn't an actual monkey.

97
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:26,280
Don't touch those bars!

98
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:29,377
How do you know they're not
bananas if you haven't eaten one?

99
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:30,300
Watch out!

100
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:38,950
It's just too tough!

101
00:05:39,033 --> 00:05:40,920
The banana didn't even ditch it!

102
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,780
Vivi, please, hurry!

103
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,420
Hey, Straw Hats.

104
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,717
We're all about to die!

105
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,377
How can you just sit there like that?

106
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:51,997
You should be trying to
get us out of here, too!

107
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,139
Tell me something.

108
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,900
How much do you guys know?

109
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,380
What exactly is Crocodile after?

110
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,660
The woman at Crocodile's side.

111
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:05,057
Did you know the world governments had a
sizable price on her head for 20 years?

112
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:08,140
As I recall, over 70 million berries.

113
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,680
70 million?

114
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,880
Holy Mellow!

115
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:12,920
But why is it so much?

116
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,137
It's almost as much as Crocodile had.

117
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,279
The moment those two joined forces,

118
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,437
this insurrection became
more than just a simple coup.

119
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,297
If they're not stopped here and now,

120
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:26,017
this could very well turn into something
the whole world would get dragged into.

121
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:27,160
The whole world?

122
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,793
Wait, what do you mean?

123
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:31,537
This is starting to sound
a little far-fetched.

124
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,561
I don't care if all that is true.

125
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,880
Huh, I don't need any other excuses.

126
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,937
I'm still gonna kick that guy's ass.

127
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:45,760
I See so how do you
intend to get out of here?

128
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,760
Wait just tough it out.

129
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,801
He says she brings some help back

130
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:06,828
Vivi, I know you're doing all
you can, but please hurry back.

131
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:11,617
Dammit, if only my swordsmanship were
better, I could cut through this stupid cage.

132
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,640
We'd be free.

133
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:18,011
It's really impolite to make a lot of
noise at mealtime like you were doing.

134
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,946
I'll teach you how to behave.

135
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,140
Bad manner, kick course!

136
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:59,440
Hey guys, been waiting long?

137
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,420
Jay, it's Mr. Prince!

138
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,617
We're finally gonna get out of here now!

139
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:05,530
Thank you.

140
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,157
Well, don't just stand there!

141
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,657
Find the key and get us out of here!

142
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,700
Mommy, my dear!

143
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,840
Do you love me now?

144
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:13,480
Oh, well...

145
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,830
Um, sure!

146
00:08:14,913 --> 00:08:18,517
And I'll love you even more if
you hurry up and open this cage!

147
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,500
He is one lovesick idiot.

148
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:22,810
Phoebe!

149
00:08:22,893 --> 00:08:23,780
All right, way to go!

150
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,980
More diners with bad manners, huh?

151
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:33,940
Get them, Saucy!

152
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:36,434
Smash those weird bananas into pudding!

153
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:44,217
Don't worry, I'm gonna teach these
bananas some proper table manners alright.

154
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:47,777
Since theirs are so bad they attacked
a lady, I'll do it the hard way.

155
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:51,757
I'll take my sweet time doing it
too, cause nobody does that to Nami.

156
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,958
We don't have any time for chivalry!

157
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,157
One second strikes!

158
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,240
No, make that one instant strikes!

159
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:00,640
The third one who just
came in has the key.

160
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,740
Hey, how do you know that, Smokey?

161
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,797
Guess your ears aren't
as big as your mouth.

162
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:09,497
Isn't that one's growl the same
as the one who swallowed the key?

163
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,051
Smart thinking collapsing the
bridge to buy time like that.

164
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,777
There are obviously more straw
hats here than we thought.

165
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:19,837
So that was all done to lure us away
so they could rescue their friends.

166
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,620
Of course it was. Hey!

167
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,310
Key!

168
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,500
There it is! Get it!

169
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,460
Hey, wait a minute!

170
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,564
That doesn't look like the key.

171
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:38,360
What's wrong?

172
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,640
What the?

173
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,760
Yes, water at last.

174
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,860
It's a miracle!

175
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:49,880
Hey, it's him.

176
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,340
Mr. Three!

177
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,040
Mr. Three?

178
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:57,242
What was he doing in the
belly of a banana Katorea?

179
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:07,777
I thought I was a goner stupid
crocodile so you thought

180
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:10,097
you could get rid of me but
you didn't try hard enough

181
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:12,917
the moment I was swallowed
I used the last of my power

182
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,657
to create that waxwax ball

183
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:21,440
that was how I survived a key

184
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:33,940
Wait, why do they want
this key so bad? Hold on.

185
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,059
A room that's surrounded
by and flooding with water.

186
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,500
A cage full of Straw Hats.

187
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,700
And they're screaming
like mad for this key.

188
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,220
Now I see what's happening here.

189
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:49,570
Mr.

190
00:10:49,653 --> 00:10:50,820
Three, I presume. Ah!

191
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,300
How'd you know who I was?

192
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,760
Well, your hairstyle gave it away.

193
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,059
I'll take the key.

194
00:10:59,160 --> 00:10:59,990
Toss it here.

195
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,190
Hmm?

196
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,340
Sure thing! Here you go!

197
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:08,650
Hey!

198
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,077
I don't know who you are,

199
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:19,877
but if you want the Straw Hats
out, you're no friend of mine.

200
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:20,790
You want the key?

201
00:11:20,873 --> 00:11:22,400
Go find it! Good luck!

202
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:24,457
You'll need it with all
those alligators around.

203
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:25,640
Trust me, I know.

204
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,010
Jerk.

205
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,957
So what happens if
their rescuer is able to

206
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,805
ascertain which banana
Katorea swallowed the key?

207
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:38,677
Huh, well, even if they were able to get
the key, it wouldn't make any difference.

208
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,477
I've had the real one with me.

209
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,457
The key in the gator's belly's a fraud,

210
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:45,177
but that's for me to know
and them to find out.

211
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:46,090
You're bad.

212
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,635
Wait a minute, Sanji.

213
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:53,033
He might be good for something, like
using those wax powers to make a key.

214
00:11:58,960 --> 00:11:59,790
You're right.

215
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,000
Nice work, Candleman.

216
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,772
Now there are just two more things to do.

217
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,070
Let's go.

218
00:12:20,153 --> 00:12:21,077
We have to hurry.

219
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:21,990
Right.

220
00:12:22,073 --> 00:12:24,037
We've got to stop the rebels
before they attack Alubarna.

221
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:26,337
We should be able to get
out through that hallway.

222
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:27,817
There's a problem with that.

223
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:29,782
Namely, dozens of banana-gators.

224
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:32,500
That's it!

225
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:35,720
I can take on hundreds
of those weird bananas!

226
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,360
Um, that problem solved.

227
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:42,544
And I had so much trouble
with just one of them.

228
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,517
No, don't be so hard on yourself.

229
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:46,817
Those two just have
crazy abnormal strength.

230
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:47,730
Yeah?

231
00:12:47,813 --> 00:12:50,461
I'd be even stronger if I
wasn't soaked right now!

232
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,070
Ah!

233
00:13:05,153 --> 00:13:06,437
This place is falling apart!

234
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,820
Yeah, we can see that!

235
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:09,410
Oh no!

236
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,345
The passageway's probably due!

237
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,794
We've got to get out of here right now!

238
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:25,950
All right,

239
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:28,737
Straw Hats time to pay if
the banana gators haven't

240
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:31,437
finished you off yet You'll
wish they had by the time.

241
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,520
I'm done with you

242
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,660
This can't be

243
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,520
Hey, you alive there, Luffy?

244
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:04,360
Usopp, please wake up!

245
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:07,120
Come on, just kick your legs or something!

246
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,380
Hey, help us pull you out of here!

247
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:14,032
Geez, why would a pirate want devil
fruit powers if it means he can't swim?

248
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,620
What? Smoker!

249
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:21,257
Hey, Zoro, what are you doing?

250
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:23,557
In case you forgot, that guy's our enemy!

251
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,470
Back off!

252
00:14:24,553 --> 00:14:28,049
I didn't want to do it, but he
was about to die, that's all.

253
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,150
Whatever.

254
00:14:30,233 --> 00:14:31,477
We gotta get moving, guys.

255
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:33,501
We've lost too much time already.

256
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,920
Vivi, can we still make it?

257
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:37,280
I don't know.

258
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,190
Hey, Nami.

259
00:14:39,273 --> 00:14:41,312
You still have that perfume I bought you?

260
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,080
Huh? Yeah. But why?

261
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:46,000
Put some of it on, please.

262
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:48,530
Okay.

263
00:14:48,613 --> 00:14:51,757
Oh, just one whiff of it makes me
swoon like a schoolboy in love.

264
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,664
I did not to mention make
you act like an idiot.

265
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,280
Why did you save my life?

266
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,480
Zoro, quick!

267
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,000
You gotta save Smokey!

268
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:26,930
What?

269
00:15:27,013 --> 00:15:27,843
He's our enemy.

270
00:15:27,926 --> 00:15:28,756
He can take care of himself.

271
00:15:28,839 --> 00:15:29,669
No, he can't.

272
00:15:29,752 --> 00:15:32,367
He's got Devil Fruit
power, so he can't swim.

273
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,217
He'll drown if you don't help him.

274
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,594
For crying out loud, Luffy,
do I really have to do this?

275
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,920
Oh, jeez.

276
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:44,559
All I did was follow my
captain's orders, that's it.

277
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:47,682
So, wouldn't read too much
into it if I were you.

278
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:50,686
It was one of his crazy
whims, pay it no mind.

279
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:57,637
Then you wouldn't have any gripes with me
carrying out my duties and arresting you,

280
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,550
right?

281
00:15:58,633 --> 00:16:00,362
See, I knew this was a bad idea.

282
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,912
This is what you get for saving a marine.

283
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:08,970
They're here?

284
00:16:09,053 --> 00:16:10,960
The Straw Hat Pirates? Yes, sir.

285
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:13,317
And it looks like they have
Captain Smoker surrounded.

286
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,720
Not for long, they won't. No way!

287
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,030
Yeah!

288
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,190
All right!

289
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,917
Full speed ahead to Alubarna!

290
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,080
There's Crocodile!

291
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,200
Let me at him!

292
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:28,740
Finally awake, huh?

293
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,420
You want some of this? Bring it on!

294
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:39,180
It's Smoker!

295
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:41,297
Luffy, forget it.

296
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:42,210
Let's just get out of here.

297
00:16:42,293 --> 00:16:43,123
Come on!

298
00:16:43,206 --> 00:16:45,380
I should, but you just saved my life.

299
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,060
This way! Hurry!

300
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:02,950
Go.

301
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:08,277
This is the only time I'm
letting you Straw Hats off.

302
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,190
Got it?

303
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:12,460
When we next meet, it's
going to be his enemies.

304
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,580
There they are!

305
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,000
Get them!

306
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:32,057
Reinforcements have
arrived, Captain Smoker!

307
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:32,970
Hold on!

308
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,900
Don't let them escape! Cut them off!

309
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,040
Well, that's our cue.

310
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:42,120
So, Vivi, which way to Alubarna? That way!

311
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:45,117
Due east across the
desert! They're running!

312
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,320
After them!

313
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:48,020
Luffy, come on.

314
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:48,950
What are you doing?

315
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:49,863
Aren't you coming?

316
00:17:49,946 --> 00:17:50,776
Yeah.

317
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:00,740
They won't escape us, men!

318
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,670
Hey!

319
00:18:04,753 --> 00:18:06,600
You're not such a bad guy, Smokey!

320
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,612
Would you get the hell out of here, Frye!

321
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,647
Don't worry, Captain Smoker!

322
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,898
We won't let those pirates get away!

323
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:58,960
I see them!

324
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:00,720
After them!

325
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:18,260
Captain, aren't you coming?

326
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:21,180
You go.

327
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:24,840
I'm tired. You're tired? Listen. Sir.

328
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,817
There's no point pursuing them now.

329
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,782
Have the men call off the chase.

330
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,460
I want everyone assembled here.

331
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:35,017
And contact headquarters.

332
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:39,037
Tell them to mobilize every military
vessel in the vicinity and route them here.

333
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,800
I want Alabasta surrounded.

334
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,494
You're calling for reinforcements, sir?

335
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:44,490
But, sir,

336
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,737
if I may point out,

337
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,577
our superiors may not
be willing to move that

338
00:19:47,660 --> 00:19:50,397
many ships against such a
small number of pirates.

339
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:53,774
And since when do I care what
the superiors might think?

340
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,070
Sorry, sir.

341
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,520
I'll get right on it.

342
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:58,170
Hey!

343
00:19:58,253 --> 00:20:00,660
The pursuit has been
called off! Come back!

344
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:15,930
Hurry!

345
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,280
Yeah, this way.

346
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:23,028
The scent of Nami's perfume is
getting stronger and stronger.

347
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:24,950
Hey!

348
00:20:25,033 --> 00:20:28,477
Please tell me you guys aren't planning
to run all the way to Alubarna!

349
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:29,860
We've got eyelash!

350
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,557
Just where the hell is
that stupid camel anyway?

351
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,660
Close, I hope.

352
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,557
Doesn't this town have a stable?

353
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,934
Let's get some horses!

354
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:41,497
But the whole town is crawling
with marines! Not to worry.

355
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,877
Look ahead.

356
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:45,300
Hey guys, come on!

357
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:49,457
A crab.

358
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:53,300
Jumper, that's a moving crab.

359
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,880
Jumby.

360
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,477
Wow, awesome!

361
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,117
I can't believe my eyes.?

362
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,680
I bet it's delicious! I'll abide!

363
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:15,620
We get to ride it!

364
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:19,140
Pleased to meet ya!

365
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:21,457
Is it just me or does its
face look kind of shady?

366
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:22,370
Who cares?

367
00:21:22,453 --> 00:21:23,632
At least we have a ride.

368
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:25,890
Say hello.

369
00:21:25,973 --> 00:21:27,154
He's Eyelash's friend.

370
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:33,617
Eyelash has lots of friends in this
area because it's his hometown.

371
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,217
He was born and raised here.

372
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:37,360
He's nice, but kind of pervy.

373
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:39,957
I can't believe you found one.

374
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:42,317
Moving crabs are always
submerged under the sand,

375
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:44,377
so it's nearly impossible to spot one.

376
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:47,277
Judging by his size, I'd
say this guy's pretty fast.

377
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:49,240
Okay, time to move out.

378
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,740
Hang on, everyone.

379
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,080
Here we go!

380
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,913
Chopper, stop the crab!

381
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:15,080
It's him!

382
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:23,600
Hey, Luffy!

383
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,020
That damn idiot!

384
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:26,500
Luffy, no!

385
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,880
You guys go on ahead!

386
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:32,420
Don't worry about me!

387
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:45,480
Make sure you deliver Vivi home!

388
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,954
Safe and sound, you have to promise me!

389
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,180
Good luck, you guys.

390
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:55,850
Idiot.

391
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:59,020
Hey, let's go, Chopper.

392
00:22:59,140 --> 00:23:02,700
Just keep going to
Alibar now. Right. Okay.

393
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,700
Let's go, crab!

394
00:23:06,060 --> 00:23:07,500
Hey, hold on!

395
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:09,420
Wait, Zoro! No!

396
00:23:09,620 --> 00:23:11,440
That's cold! Stop the crab!

397
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,420
We gotta go back!

398
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:14,980
It's all right, Vivi.

399
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:15,930
He'll be fine.

400
00:23:16,013 --> 00:23:17,557
You have to trust me on this, okay?

401
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,897
I certainly feel sorry for the other guy.

402
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:21,921
Luffy shows no mercy to his prey.

403
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:26,357
And there's not a single person he's
gone after that was able to walk away.

404
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,616
Crocodile will fail.

405
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:28,680
Luffy will win.

406
00:23:29,180 --> 00:23:30,420
It's that simple.

407
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:36,200
The moment that the Rebel Army started
running, this land's final hour was set.

408
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:40,680
Once the Royal Army and the
Rebel Army meet, this country,

409
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:43,666
the Kingdom of Alabasta,
will be gone forever.

410
00:23:44,460 --> 00:23:48,217
If you truly are the one and only
hope for preventing that tragedy,

411
00:23:48,300 --> 00:23:50,660
then you must survive, no matter what.

412
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,960
So, from this moment forward,

413
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:59,160
what happens to Luffy, or any of us for
that matter, isn't the least bit important.

414
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:02,490
But...

415
00:24:05,420 --> 00:24:08,720
Vivi, this is a fight that
you and you alone started.

416
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:13,097
You're the one who bravely left
this land years ago and made

417
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:17,004
the decision to stand up against
a corrupt and evil organization.

418
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:23,624
However, don't make the mistake
of thinking you're alone anymore.

419
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:28,180
Yeah, that's right! Don't worry!

420
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:31,820
Because, because Captain
Usopp is going to protect you!

421
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:33,730
Luffy!

422
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:39,190
Listen!

423
00:24:39,273 --> 00:24:40,960
We'll be waiting for you!

424
00:24:41,260 --> 00:24:42,840
We'll be in our moment!

425
00:24:43,740 --> 00:24:44,570
Yeah!

426
00:24:55,700 --> 00:24:58,994
You could say Princess Vivi
slipped through our fingers.

427
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:03,700
No matter, the agents are still
scheduled to gather in Alubarna.

428
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:05,820
Contact them at once.

429
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:14,060
Strawhat, I'd say you've taken
this nonsense a little too far.

430
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,230
Nonsense.

431
00:25:19,313 --> 00:25:20,706
Vivi doesn't see it that way.

432
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:24,507
You see, unlike most people, she
genuinely cares about others.

433
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:27,997
I guess deep down she's an optimist.

434
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:29,904
Even if it's not too realistic.

435
00:25:30,180 --> 00:25:31,945
Take this revolt, for example.

436
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:34,021
She believes no one needs to die.

437
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:35,600
Nobody needs to die.

438
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:40,677
The problem with idealistic fools
like Princess Vivi is they take a

439
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:44,637
stand without any comprehension of
what is truly involved in a real fight.

440
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:45,838
Wouldn't you agree?

441
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,070
Yep.

442
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:52,917
But that doesn't change the fact
that as long as you're around,

443
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:56,294
Vivi's gonna fight until she
either wins or dies trying.

444
00:25:58,080 --> 00:26:01,580
So I figure, I'll take
you down right here!

445
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:06,600
Such a foolish boy.

446
00:26:07,220 --> 00:26:11,044
Despite what the idealists cry
about, there's one constant truth.

447
00:26:11,140 --> 00:26:14,760
On the rough battlefields of
life, you either kill or die.

448
00:26:15,420 --> 00:26:17,377
That's why I'm more than happy to shoot a

449
00:26:17,460 --> 00:26:19,989
bullet through every
bleeding heart I meet.

450
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:24,740
Yeah, which proves you're
the bigger fool here.

451
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,297
you think something's funny?

452
00:26:31,380 --> 00:26:33,797
perhaps you'd like to die as well?

453
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:38,497
nico robin if you want
to try go right ahead and

454
00:26:38,580 --> 00:26:40,777
didn't you promise not
to call me by that name?

455
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:42,437
where are you going?

456
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,357
i'm headed to Alubarna see you there?

457
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:48,420
damn woman i'll never figure her out.

458
00:26:51,580 --> 00:26:53,560
i've got three minutes to spare.

459
00:26:57,260 --> 00:26:58,217
after that?

460
00:26:58,300 --> 00:27:01,620
i'm certain your time
will have run out as well.

461
00:27:10,320 --> 00:27:11,780
it's your move, kid.

462
00:27:13,420 --> 00:27:14,537
with pleasure.

463
00:27:14,620 --> 00:27:18,360
Gum-Gum!

464
00:27:18,580 --> 00:27:19,880
HIT GUM!

465
00:27:32,620 --> 00:27:34,040
And Gum-Gum!

466
00:27:46,540 --> 00:27:50,017
by now it should be quite
obvious but i'll warn you

467
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:55,620
you cannot defeat me this is
an exercise in Utility. Stop!

468
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:57,330
Get me!

469
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:17,660
Listen to my warning and take heed.

470
00:28:17,980 --> 00:28:20,215
If you continue this senseless attack?

471
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:22,097
You will have accomplished nothing.

472
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:24,940
and wasted what little time you have left.

473
00:28:46,980 --> 00:28:51,340
Good critics, you lousy old sandgator!

474
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:56,680
You're wasting your time, boy.

475
00:28:58,340 --> 00:28:59,380
You bastard!

476
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,237
No matter how hard you
fight against the truth,

477
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:06,261
there's no way a rubber freak like
you could even hope to rival me.

478
00:29:09,220 --> 00:29:11,660
I'm sorry, my fist interrupted you.

479
00:29:11,780 --> 00:29:12,898
Now, what was that?

480
00:29:22,180 --> 00:29:25,020
I've had my fill of your
pathetic fun and games.

481
00:29:26,740 --> 00:29:29,040
Let's end this, now. Fun and games!

482
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:30,828
Trust me, I'm dead serious!

483
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:32,150
Jerk!

484
00:29:32,233 --> 00:29:33,457
Dammit, he's right, though.

485
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:35,857
He's got an answer for all of my attacks.

486
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,180
What do I do now?

487
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:41,500
We may both be pirates, but you
fall grossly short on skill.

488
00:29:42,980 --> 00:29:43,940
Desert Spada!

489
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:57,700
Nice reflexes, boy.

490
00:29:58,040 --> 00:30:01,158
A full-on hit from that
attack would have killed you.

491
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,780
What the?

492
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:05,660
That's one deep hole!

493
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:10,478
You may have Devil Fruit powers, but
you lack discipline and training.

494
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:13,217
With that, your skills could
be as formidable as any.

495
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:14,771
But you're not there yet.

496
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:18,097
Like so many fools, you waste time
obsessing over your abilities.

497
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:22,880
Gimmicks get you only so far in a fight
without the skill sets to back them up.

498
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:28,140
Desert Gyrosol!

499
00:30:40,580 --> 00:30:41,657
What in the...?

500
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:43,180
What's going on?!

501
00:30:49,300 --> 00:30:50,260
The sand!

502
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:51,380
It's sinking!

503
00:30:51,700 --> 00:30:52,600
What is this?

504
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:58,220
What is this stuff? Let me out!

505
00:30:58,340 --> 00:30:59,170
Let me out!

506
00:30:59,253 --> 00:31:00,083
Let me out!

507
00:31:00,166 --> 00:31:00,996
Let me out! What's wrong?

508
00:31:01,079 --> 00:31:02,391
Never heard of quicksand?

509
00:31:02,600 --> 00:31:05,417
It makes for a convenient
desert burial when

510
00:31:05,500 --> 00:31:07,537
you need to get rid of someone in a hurry.

511
00:31:07,620 --> 00:31:10,497
The sand is drawn down
into underground waterways,

512
00:31:10,580 --> 00:31:14,377
and I have the good fortune of being
able to detect exactly where they are.

513
00:31:14,460 --> 00:31:19,225
That advantage alone is enough to make me
unbeatable when fighting in the desert.

514
00:31:21,780 --> 00:31:27,020
If you think I'm going to let myself
be buried alive in this sand trap,

515
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:29,082
you've got another thing coming!

516
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:30,740
You bastard!

517
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:32,840
I'm gone!

518
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:41,660
If I can't flunk you, then
maybe I could catch you instead!

519
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,740
I'm gone, shit!

520
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:50,040
HAVEN'T YOU LEARNED
ANYTHING, MORON, PREDICTABLE?

521
00:31:50,600 --> 00:31:52,140
Shut up, gum -

522
00:31:55,060 --> 00:31:57,960
This is really getting old.

523
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:01,290
LET ME GO!

524
00:32:01,373 --> 00:32:02,480
I'M FLORTING YOU!

525
00:32:02,780 --> 00:32:03,820
CHRISTEN CUTLIN

526
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:09,430
MY...

527
00:32:09,513 --> 00:32:10,840
MY ARM!

528
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:17,800
What did you do?

529
00:32:18,060 --> 00:32:20,500
It's all shriveled up like a mummy!

530
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:22,517
You turned my arm into a mummy!

531
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,430
Stop whining.

532
00:32:23,513 --> 00:32:24,840
This is the price you pay.

533
00:32:25,100 --> 00:32:27,857
The sand has absorbed all
the moisture from your arm.

534
00:32:27,940 --> 00:32:28,800
You're lucky.

535
00:32:29,100 --> 00:32:31,257
All I decided to attack was your arm.

536
00:32:31,340 --> 00:32:35,020
I can do this all day long,
until you're a pile of dust.

537
00:32:37,460 --> 00:32:39,520
You gotta be kidding me!

538
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:42,760
That's it! Water!

539
00:32:49,780 --> 00:32:50,880
All in vain.

540
00:32:51,340 --> 00:32:52,860
You're wrong, Sandy!

541
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:56,920
You see, that old guy in Yuba
gave me this barrel of water.

542
00:32:57,040 --> 00:32:59,177
He spent all night
digging it up just for me!

543
00:32:59,260 --> 00:33:01,680
Luffy, here, take this with you.

544
00:33:02,100 --> 00:33:04,440
He's not scared and neither am I!

545
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:09,880
I'm not about to give in to
the sand without a fight!

546
00:33:10,100 --> 00:33:10,980
Gum-Gum!

547
00:33:12,180 --> 00:33:13,840
This is getting ridiculous.

548
00:33:14,460 --> 00:33:15,600
My spine!

549
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,030
Enough!

550
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:24,460
This fails now!

551
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:31,660
Vermin, it is time to die.

552
00:33:31,900 --> 00:33:34,194
Both you and the accursed land of Yuba.

553
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:37,840
Your three minutes are up.

554
00:33:38,040 --> 00:33:42,687
Like I said at the start, I don't have
time to fool around with you any longer.

555
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:45,640
Now, Sables!

556
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:05,080
Ah, the sand so soothing and dry.

557
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:07,580
Look out! Sandstorm!

558
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:09,057
Right ahead in the sky!

559
00:34:09,140 --> 00:34:09,970
Take shelter!

560
00:34:10,100 --> 00:34:10,930
Wait a minute!

561
00:34:11,013 --> 00:34:12,586
No, it's not coming this way!

562
00:34:12,700 --> 00:34:13,537
It's headed south!

563
00:34:13,620 --> 00:34:16,100
Captain Smoker, look! Up there!

564
00:34:22,100 --> 00:34:23,680
Vivi! What's wrong?

565
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:26,666
There's a giant storm
moving toward Rain Base!

566
00:34:28,040 --> 00:34:29,400
It's Crocodile!

567
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:33,920
Luffy, no!

568
00:34:43,020 --> 00:34:43,977
Listen carefully.

569
00:34:44,060 --> 00:34:45,277
Can you hear it move?

570
00:34:45,360 --> 00:34:49,301
In this land, the prevailing winds
always blow from north to south.

571
00:34:49,560 --> 00:34:50,460
And so,

572
00:34:50,720 --> 00:34:55,057
if this infantile sandstorm of mine
were to, say, catch one of these winds,

573
00:34:55,140 --> 00:34:57,997
it would grow exponentially
until it became a monster.

574
00:34:58,080 --> 00:35:01,877
And following its trajectory south,
where do you think it would strike?

575
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:02,790
Tell me!

576
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:05,460
Then Yuba.

577
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:10,240
No, not there!

578
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:14,700
Dammit, why the hell are
you doing this? Stop it!

579
00:35:15,540 --> 00:35:17,160
Look, it started.

580
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:18,499
It's headed south.

581
00:35:18,780 --> 00:35:22,251
That nice old man has nothing
to do with this, you hear me?

582
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:25,880
Stop it or I swear I'll
kill you, you bastard!

583
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:29,820
You leave that old man alone!

584
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:37,300
You cannot alter fate that sandstorm
is going to pick up strength.

585
00:35:38,180 --> 00:35:42,037
And eventually it will become strong
enough that even I can't stop it.

586
00:35:42,120 --> 00:35:44,160
I don't believe you! Liar.

587
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:47,077
Yuba is finished.

588
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:48,417
You don't end this now.

589
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:49,600
I will.

590
00:35:59,820 --> 00:36:02,114
Did you really think you were my equal?

591
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:11,040
There have been any number of rookies
like you who've challenged me.

592
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:14,820
And you've all shared a common
trait, fatal ineptitude.

593
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:21,860
And in the end, the only thing you
are truly qualified for is death.
